{
  "courseSlug": "understanding-house-rent-allowance-hra-tax-exemption",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "title": "Chapter 2: Calculating Your HRA Exemption",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "title": "Worked Examples: HRA Calculations Across Salary Levels and Cities",
          "slug": "worked-examples-hra-calculations-across-salary-levels-and-cities",
          "body": [
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-001",
              "_type": "bigIdea",
              "text": "The same three-limit rule gives very different results for a trainee in Indore and a banker in Mumbai. Working through real salary profiles is the fastest way to build an instinct for which limit binds, what the exemption is worth and when it tips the regime choice."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-002",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-002s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "This lesson is almost entirely numbers. Five employees, five cities, five pay levels, all in tax year 2026-27. For each one, we calculate the exempt HRA, then go one step further than most guides: we work out the actual tax saved using old regime slabs, and compare it with what the same person would pay under the new regime.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-003",
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "warning",
              "text": "Assumptions used throughout: resident individuals below 60, salary as the only income, standard deduction of ₹50,000 under the old regime and ₹75,000 under the new regime, 4% cess, figures unchanged all year, and no professional tax. Taxes are rounded to the nearest rupee."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-004",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-004s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Profile 1: The Graduate Trainee",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-005",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-005s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Arpit, Graduate trainee, Indore",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-006",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-006s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Basic ₹20,000 a month, HRA ₹8,000, special allowance ₹12,000, gross ₹40,000. He shares a flat in Vijay Nagar and pays ₹9,000 a month as his share. Section 80C: ₹28,800 (his own PF).",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-007",
              "_type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Limit",
                "Working",
                "Amount"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-007r1",
                  "cells": [
                    "1. HRA received",
                    "₹8,000 × 12",
                    "₹96,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-007r2",
                  "cells": [
                    "2. Rent minus 10% of salary",
                    "₹1,08,000 minus ₹24,000",
                    "₹84,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-007r3",
                  "cells": [
                    "3. 40% of salary (Indore)",
                    "40% of ₹2,40,000",
                    "₹96,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-007r4",
                  "cells": [
                    "Exempt HRA",
                    "Smallest: Limit 2",
                    "₹84,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-007r5",
                  "cells": [
                    "Taxable HRA",
                    "₹96,000 minus ₹84,000",
                    "₹12,000"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-008",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-008s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "His exemption is ₹84,000, but it saves him ₹0 in tax. Without HRA, his old regime taxable income is ₹4,01,200, which is already below ₹5 lakh, so the rebate cancels his tax. Under the new regime his taxable income of ₹4,05,000 is also tax-free. For Arpit, HRA paperwork is a formality with no rupee value this year.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-009",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-009s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Profile 2: The Mid-Level Engineer",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-010",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-010s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Sreeja, Software engineer, Kochi",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-011",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-011s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Basic ₹45,000 a month, HRA ₹18,000 (40% of basic), special allowance ₹27,000, gross ₹90,000. She rents a 1BHK in Kakkanad for ₹20,000 a month. Section 80C: ₹1,50,000.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-012",
              "_type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Limit",
                "Working",
                "Amount"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-012r1",
                  "cells": [
                    "1. HRA received",
                    "₹18,000 × 12",
                    "₹2,16,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-012r2",
                  "cells": [
                    "2. Rent minus 10% of salary",
                    "₹2,40,000 minus ₹54,000",
                    "₹1,86,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-012r3",
                  "cells": [
                    "3. 40% of salary (Kochi)",
                    "40% of ₹5,40,000",
                    "₹2,16,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-012r4",
                  "cells": [
                    "Exempt HRA",
                    "Smallest: Limit 2",
                    "₹1,86,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-012r5",
                  "cells": [
                    "Taxable HRA",
                    "₹2,16,000 minus ₹1,86,000",
                    "₹30,000"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-013",
              "_type": "comparison",
              "title": "Sreeja: what her ₹1,86,000 exemption is worth",
              "columns": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-cmpB-1",
                  "label": "Old regime",
                  "points": [
                    "Taxable income without HRA: ₹8,80,000, tax ₹92,040",
                    "Taxable income with HRA: ₹6,94,000, tax ₹53,352",
                    "Tax saved by HRA: ₹38,688"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-cmpB-2",
                  "label": "New regime",
                  "points": [
                    "Taxable income: ₹10,05,000",
                    "Tax after rebate: ₹0",
                    "HRA not allowed, and not needed"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-014",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-014s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "HRA genuinely saves Sreeja ₹38,688 under the old regime, about 20.8% of her exemption because it comes off her 20% slab. But she pays nothing at all under the new regime. The exemption is real, the saving is not.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-015",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-015s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Profile 3: The Government Officer",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-016",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-016s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Venkat, Central government officer (Level 11), Hyderabad",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-017",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-017s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Basic ₹67,700 a month, DA at 60% ₹40,620, HRA at 30% of basic ₹20,310, gross ₹1,28,630. He rents in Kukatpally for ₹30,000 a month. Salary for HRA includes DA: ₹1,08,320 a month. Section 80C: ₹1,50,000.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-018",
              "_type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Limit",
                "Working",
                "Amount"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-018r1",
                  "cells": [
                    "1. HRA received",
                    "₹20,310 × 12",
                    "₹2,43,720"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-018r2",
                  "cells": [
                    "2. Rent minus 10% of salary",
                    "₹3,60,000 minus ₹1,29,984",
                    "₹2,30,016"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-018r3",
                  "cells": [
                    "3. 50% of salary (Hyderabad)",
                    "50% of ₹12,99,840",
                    "₹6,49,920"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-018r4",
                  "cells": [
                    "Exempt HRA",
                    "Smallest: Limit 2",
                    "₹2,30,016"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-018r5",
                  "cells": [
                    "Taxable HRA",
                    "₹2,43,720 minus ₹2,30,016",
                    "₹13,704"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-019",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-019s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Limit 3 is huge at ₹6,49,920 because DA lifts salary and Hyderabad is now a 50% city, but it is irrelevant: his modest rent makes Limit 2 the binding limit. HRA saves him ₹71,765 under the old regime. His taxable income stays above ₹10 lakh both with and without the exemption (₹13,43,560 and ₹11,13,544), so the whole exemption is saved at 30% plus cess. His old regime tax with HRA is ₹1,52,426. The new regime charges ₹1,04,295. The new regime wins.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l4-020",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l4-020s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Profile 4: The Engineering Manager",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
